  "slug": "learning-reconstruction-galaxy-a30c",
  "summary": "Five preprints extend redshift-space, field-level, lensing and systematics-deprojection methods to extract more field information from galaxy and lensing data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reconstructing underlying fields from observables through explicit statistical modelling of higher-order or field-level information. In redshift space, a tracer-centred density-split model derives bias and an empirical cosmological description, while the isotropic galaxy 4PCF is shown to have vanishing parity-odd redshift-space distortion contributions after line-of-sight averaging. A faster field-level likelihood for large-scale galaxy surveys forecasts sigma(fNL)=4.1. In weak lensing, roulette amplitudes beyond flexion improve least-squares lens-mass reconstruction for clusters. For SPHEREx, an information-criterion-driven, non-linear deprojection addresses angular imaging systematics, tested on lognormal mocks. What is new is the focus on analytic, likelihood-based and systematics-aware treatment of the field, rather than compression alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
